    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44649" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐόφθαλμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with beautiful eyes</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.1.41
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			), <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				316.14
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>keen-eyed</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				5.5
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>pleasing to the eye</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aristox.
				<u>Fr.Hist.</u>
				15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cat.Cod.Astr.</u>
				8(4).240
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>fair only to the eye, specious</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐόφθαλμον ἀκοῦσαι μόνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1268b24
				</span></i>
			. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μως</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				<u>Fr.</u>
				59
			</span></i>.</div>
